<title>PORTUGAL: Small investors push Lisnave higher.</title>
<headline>Small investors push Lisnave higher.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Small investors pushed Portuguese ship repairer Lisnave-Estaleiros Navais de Lisboa, a generally illiquid stock, higher on the Lisbon bourse, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;If anyone believes the share is going to be volatile, buy orders appear,&quot; said one operator.</p>
<p>Lisnave stood at 331 escudos, up 23, in volume of 141,300 shares at 1413 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Paula Cordeiro, Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
